# Project structure

Solution layout and layer boundaries: **`architecture-conventions.mdc`**. This rule covers **WebApp** (`src/WebApp/`) only.

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| **Endpoints/** | MVC controllers `*Endpoints.cs`. Register via `MapControllers` in `Startup.cs`. |
| **Components/** | Blazor UI. See `blazor-conventions.mdc`. |
| **Features/** | CQRS use cases (`WebApp.Features.*`) + `IFeatureSender`. One file per use case: Request, validator, handler, Response. See `data-conventions.mdc`. |
| **AI/** | MAF agents, tools, `ChatOrchestrator`. See `ai-conventions.mdc`. |
| **Models/** | App/UI models (`AppResult`, unmigrated form DTOs, mail/AI types). Feature-owned Request/Response live in **Features/** — see `dto-conventions.mdc`. |
| **Utilities/** | Extensions, Helpers, Services (`UserMailboxService`, `CurrentUser`). No MailKit — mailbox adapter is in Infrastructure. |

**Not in WebApp anymore:** `AppDbContext`, `Persistence`, entities (`Core/Entities/`), repository DTOs (`Core/DTOs/`).

## Endpoints

- One file per area: `AuthEndpoints.cs`, etc. Namespace `WebApp.Endpoints`.
- HTTP under `/api/...`; Blazor routes under `/...`.

Do not put HTTP routes under `Components/` or `Features/` handlers.

## Utilities

| Subfolder | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| **Extensions/** | `{Concern}Extensions.cs` — class name matches file |
| **Helpers/** | `{Concern}Helpers.cs` — static utilities |
| **Services/** | DI types (`IMailboxService`, `UserMailboxService`, `CurrentUser`) |

Do not put EF `DbContext` or repository implementations under Utilities.

## AI boundaries

- **Agents/** — LLM runners; `SupportedUserPrompts` catalog per agent.
- **Tools/** — MAF tools; no LLM routing.
- **ChatOrchestrator.cs** — turn routing; uses `IChatMessageRepository` for history.
- Agents inject **`IFoundryAgentFactory`** (`Infrastructure/Foundry/FoundryAgentFactory.cs`); config type **`FoundryOptions`** in `Core/DTOs/Foundry.cs`.
- AI request/response DTOs: `WebApp/Models/AI.cs` — not under `AI/` folder.

## Foundry auth

- `Foundry:Enabled`, `Foundry:Endpoint`, `Foundry:ApiKey` in user secrets / env — never commit keys.

## Startup

- `InjectData` → `AddInfrastructure(configuration)` + `UserMailboxService`.
- `InjectFeatures` → `AddFeatureLayer()` + `IFeatureSender`.
- `InjectAi` → agents, tools, orchestrator + `Configure<FoundryOptions>`.
